From 2024a93d6cfe7fc121ed18efa23429ee1bb9fd7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:19:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09268/11362] Switch on the repetition control this run was
 missing, and decline the re-ask that comes with it

Two independent teammate evidence reports plus the Fable review converged on the
same gap, and it is aimed at exactly this run's failure mode.

WHAT WAS OFF. `_engine_induce_call = bool(codeonly_eligible) and "engine" in
required` (arc_executable_world_model.py:6885) gates `repeat_penalty=1.1,
repeat_last_n=256` (:6922-6926). The driver passed codeonly_eligible=False, so the
run had NO decode-level repetition control -- against a failure mode that is
almost entirely `stop_type=limit`. The code names that gap itself: "the
decode-level repetition loop that is the dominant induce failure" (:6918-6920).

MEASURED (docs/research-notes/arc-induce-repeat-penalty-confirm-2026-07-31.md, 36
paired attempts, gemma-4-31B):
    usable engines     13/36 -> 22/36   (1.69x; its own corrigendum C1 records the
                                         headline wrongly said "triples")
    hit the token cap  20/36 -> 2/36    <- our dominant failure mode
    missing_return     13    -> 2
    wall per attempt   100.3s -> 47.2s
Sign test p=0.049 attempt-matched, p=0.125 clustered by game.

HONEST LIMIT, from the same note: quality did NOT move. The strict out-of-sample
funnel was 4/18 vs 4/18. This buys usable engines, not better ones -- and a run
producing engines that hit the cap cannot be measuring induction quality either
way.

IT IS NOT A PROMPT CHANGE. With think mode on (the shipped default),
codeonly_eligible=True routes into generate()'s `_think_on` branch -- "no
directive, no pre-opened fence" (:6873-6874) -- so the prompt text is
byte-identical to the previous cells. Only the sampler payload changes. Symmetric
across arms.

DEFECT RE-ASK DECLINED. codeonly_eligible=True would also arm the defect re-ask,
which is documented converting an accept into a HARD FAILURE on 17 of 21 cells
against 1 of 22 control (:7035-7043, reproduced deterministically in
tests/python/test_arc_goal_defect_reask_wiring.py). Penalty and re-ask ship
independently (:4254), so all three arms now set
CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_DEFECT_REASKS=0. Measured split from the same source: "the
penalty carries 11 of the 13 paired wins, the re-ask 2" -- we are taking the 11
and declining the risk.

CONTEXT THAT RAISES THE STAKES. The 11-0-2 that retired Qwen3.6 and installed
gemma was BUDGET EXHAUSTION, not induction skill: all 18 Qwen failures were
`HIT n_predict=16384 OUTPUT LIMIT`, and exp6021's own budget_exhaustion_finding
says it "does NOT establish that Qwen is intrinsically the weaker INDUCER". The
original migration measured the same starvation this re-measurement exists to
avoid.

Also noting a citation of mine that was weaker than I represented: I twice cited
exp6199 as evidence think mode helps gemma. The de-confounded rerun exp6221 gives
1 win / 0 losses / 12 ties, p=1.0, gate NOT MET -- and exp6199 was confounded by an
`os.environ.pop` that let both arms resolve think-ON.

Ninth restart. Verified before launching: repeat_penalty=1.1, repeat_last_n=256,
defect_reasks=0.
---
 ...xperiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py | 28 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py b/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
index 4207edbf71..6838c08500 100644
--- a/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
+++ b/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
@@ -567,8 +567,34 @@ def main() -> int:
         # returned ok=True with both symbols at tries=3 (2,786 s) and overran at tries=1.
         #
         # Symmetric: both arms get 3. Gemma will simply not need the extra two.
+        # codeonly_eligible=True, to switch ON the repetition control this run was missing.
+        #
+        # WHAT IT DOES *NOT* DO: it does not restore the fence or the codeonly directive. With
+        # think mode on (the shipped default), generate() routes into its `_think_on` branch --
+        # "no directive, no pre-opened fence" (arc_executable_world_model.py:6873-6874) -- so the
+        # PROMPT TEXT IS BYTE-IDENTICAL to what the previous cells saw. This is not a prompt
+        # change.
+        #
+        # WHAT IT DOES DO: `_engine_induce_call = bool(codeonly_eligible) and "engine" in required`
+        # (:6885) gates `repeat_penalty=1.1, repeat_last_n=256` (:6922-6926). With False we were
+        # running with NO decode-level repetition control at all, against a failure mode that is
+        # almost entirely `stop_type=limit`.
+        #
+        # MEASURED, docs/research-notes/arc-induce-repeat-penalty-confirm-2026-07-31.md, 36 paired
+        # attempts on gemma-4-31B:
+        #     usable engines      13/36 -> 22/36  (1.69x, NOT the "triples" its own headline
+        #                                          claimed -- corrigendum C1 in that note)
+        #     hit the token cap   20/36 -> 2/36   <- our dominant failure mode
+        #     missing_return      13    -> 2
+        #     wall per attempt    100.3s -> 47.2s
+        # Attempt-matched sign test p=0.049; clustered by game p=0.125. HONEST LIMIT: quality did
+        # NOT move -- the strict out-of-sample funnel was 4/18 vs 4/18. This buys usable engines,
+        # not better ones.
+        #
+        # Symmetric: both arms take the same path, and gemma's own numbers above are where the
+        # effect was measured.
         ok_, code_ = prop_.generate(
-            prompt, ("engine", "is_level_complete"), tries=LIVE_TRIES, codeonly_eligible=False
+            prompt, ("engine", "is_level_complete"), tries=LIVE_TRIES, codeonly_eligible=True
         )
         if not ok_:
             return False, code_
